WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
Four workers died at TSMC's Kaohsiung fab site, halting steelwork across Taiwan. This is AI Chips &amp; Data Centres, episode 30. After the Kaohsiung halt, an edge microcontroller announcement, a memory supply warning from Dell, then power and foundry moves, a tear down on optical test, and the date sitting ahead. The dead men were on Taiwan's semiconductor manufacturing's fab 22 job in Nanzi District, inside the southern Taiwan science park. Taipei Times reports

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:34.900
the Kaushung Fire Department took the call at 4.53 a.m. in the afternoon yesterday.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.500
After four people were injured and sent 10 vehicles and 22 people.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.660
A steel structure failed during hoisting and installation.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.600
The southern Taiwan Science Park Bureau's early read is that bolts on a connecting plate

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.180
of an outer steel frame on the third floor snapped,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.200
and the workers fell with the steel.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.480
Three were pronounced dead last night.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.580
The fourth, surname Huang, died in intensive care this morning.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:01.260
All four worked for a domestic contractor.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:06.080
The independent carries TSMC's statement that the company and the contractor stopped

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:10.800
the related work on that site and stopped the same kind of steel structure work at every

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.180
TSMC construction site in Taiwan until the investigation is done.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.600
The Bureau has labor inspectors on cause and liability.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.600
Fab-22 is the fab scheduled for two nanometer chips and anything more advanced than that.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:32.322
Synaptics has introduced a part it is calling an XMCU, the Astra SR200 series, announced

00:01:32.322 --> 00:01:34.762
rather than described as in customer's hands.

00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:40.802
Tech PowerUp's account of the launch says the point is multimodal edge AI that a normal

00:01:40.802 --> 00:01:43.522
microcontroller cannot keep in on-chip memory.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:49.702
The announced design puts heterogeneous AI compute next to custom DRAM in the package, and

00:01:49.702 --> 00:01:53.082
that DRAM is described as scaling into the hundreds of megabytes.

00:01:53.082 --> 00:01:59.002
The AI block is Synaptix's torque engine, plus the Coral NPU from Google Research.

00:01:59.622 --> 00:02:05.642
Synaptix says this is the first time an ARM Cortex M85 has been paired with a Cortex M52.

00:02:06.482 --> 00:02:12.082
EE times from Synaptix Tech Day in San Jose on October 20th puts the family at up

00:02:12.082 --> 00:02:19.162
to 400 giga operations per second and 256 megabytes of that custom DRAM with vision, audio,

00:02:19.162 --> 00:02:21.282
and hardware-rooted security on the die.

00:02:21.902 --> 00:02:23.822
Three pin compatible tiers are named.

00:02:24.422 --> 00:02:30.122
SR 210 is 200 GB operations per second, aimed at always-on voice and sensing.

00:02:30.882 --> 00:02:35.542
SR 230 is 300, and adds vision, display, and optional audio.

00:02:36.262 --> 00:02:40.862
SR 250 is 400, with two vision paths and two display paths.

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:47.302
The intended boxes are wearables, battery sensors, connected cameras, streamers, and industrial

00:02:47.302 --> 00:02:48.502
visual vision and voice gear.

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:55.322
John Wile, who runs IoT and Edge AI processors at Synaptics, said the traction so far is

00:02:55.322 --> 00:02:57.422
strongest in electronics worn on the body.

00:02:58.452 --> 00:03:04.032
Socionect is pushing agentic AI out of front-end chip design and into physical design of large

00:03:04.032 --> 00:03:07.452
advanced node system on chips, working with Cadence.

00:03:08.112 --> 00:03:12.912
Semiconductor Digest reports the first target is physical design of a large 3 nanometer

00:03:12.912 --> 00:03:19.032
SAUACI using Cadence's InnoStack AI super agent with a plan to spread that agent across

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.472
more SAUACI projects.

00:03:20.932 --> 00:03:26.172
The plumbing socio-next names is retrieval augmented generation, model context protocol

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:32.052
support, custom AI skills, and agents aimed at floor planning, custom timing checks, and

00:03:32.052 --> 00:03:34.052
checklist automation still on the roadmap.

00:03:34.692 --> 00:03:39.712
President and Chief Operating Officer Hisato Yoshida said the company expects up to a five

00:03:39.712 --> 00:03:43.292
times productivity gain from Cadence's agentic workflow.

00:03:43.892 --> 00:03:48.772
Cadence's Qin Chi Tang, senior vice president, described InnoStack as open enough that

00:03:48.772 --> 00:03:50.552
a customer can load its own methods.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:56.760
An NTT-advised consortium is developing mass production technology for optical chiplets.

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.920
Semi-conductor digest reports.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.400
The companies in the group do the development.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.180
NTT's role as stated is advisor.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.400
This is a development program, not a factory start.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:13.101
Amazon has pledged 16 billion euros of investment in Germany in 2027.

00:04:14.181 --> 00:04:19.061
DataCenterDynamics says that Pledge covers more data centers and AI infrastructure, high-speed

00:04:19.061 --> 00:04:20.781
satellite internet, and logistics.

00:04:21.401 --> 00:04:26.081
It is a pledged year of spending, not a named campus that has been energized, and the

00:04:26.081 --> 00:04:27.981
euros are not split out to one site.

00:04:28.969 --> 00:04:34.229
Central Georgia Electric Membership Corporation plans a 50-megawatt deployment of home batteries.

00:04:34.229 --> 00:04:34.789
utilities.

00:04:34.789 --> 00:04:39.129
Utility Dive says the batteries are meant to cut system peaks and energy costs while

00:04:39.129 --> 00:04:42.369
hyper-scale data centers try to connect to that cooperative's grid.

00:04:43.029 --> 00:04:47.729
Those 50 megawatts are storage on the utility side, not IT load inside a hall.

00:04:48.806 --> 00:04:54.346
OVH Cloud told its annual earnings call it has 110 megawatts of data center capacity it

00:04:54.346 --> 00:04:55.966
can use to grow the customer base.

00:04:56.606 --> 00:04:57.986
Data Center Dynamics reports.

00:04:58.686 --> 00:05:03.166
That is capacity the operator says it can sell, not a new site breaking ground.

00:05:03.166 --> 00:05:08.770
1. Michael Dell told the Wall Street Journal the memory shortage gets worse next year, because

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:13.950
AI data center construction keeps taking DRAM and high-batten with memory. Techpower

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:19.590
up puts Dell's undelivered AI server orders at about $95 billion, which Dell called

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:24.730
the largest backlog the company has had, and says memory is the constraint, not orders.

00:05:25.350 --> 00:05:30.130
The accelerators in those servers want high-batten with memory. The servers around them still

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:31.470
want ordinary DRAM.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:37.450
Dell is buying DRAM only when final assembly is close, and is signing long-term supply deals.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:43.410
Techpower uplines Dell's view up with Micron's chief executive, who said supply will be much

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:50.650
tighter in 2027 and 2028 than this year, and with SK Heinex's chief executive, who expects

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:52.730
the shortage to run through 2030.

00:05:53.765 --> 00:05:58.805
Micron is putting strategic money into Indian corporations so Indian can expand refining

00:05:58.805 --> 00:06:04.365
and high-purity materials work in Rome, New York, and restart domestic processing of critical

00:06:04.365 --> 00:06:06.185
minerals used in advanced chips.

00:06:06.925 --> 00:06:11.765
Semiconductor digest ties the check to a plan micron announced in July to invest up to

00:06:11.765 --> 00:06:14.925
$3 billion in the U.S. Semiconductor supply chain.

00:06:15.565 --> 00:06:19.325
A long-term supply agreement is how micron gets access to those minerals.

00:06:20.025 --> 00:06:24.985
Chief procurement officer Ben Tesson connected that access to micron's technology roadmap,

00:06:24.985 --> 00:06:28.905
and to depending less on refining capacity concentrated overseas.

00:06:29.645 --> 00:06:34.825
Micron also restated that its expected U.S. fab and technology spend rises to more than

00:06:34.825 --> 00:06:37.805
$250 billion through 2035.

00:06:38.685 --> 00:06:43.725
Governor Kathy Hockle said the Clay Fab project is months ahead of schedule and called it the

00:06:43.725 --> 00:06:46.305
largest private investment in New York State history.

00:06:47.342 --> 00:06:52.102
Yesterday's TSMC process item was another three nanometer fab planned in Tynan.

00:06:52.102 --> 00:06:57.162
Today's plan is three nanometer production at the second factory of Japan Advanced

00:06:57.162 --> 00:07:03.122
Semiconductor Manufacturing, the Kumamoto Joint Venture, and it is a plan, not waifers moving.

00:07:03.742 --> 00:07:08.222
Electronics for you reports total equipment investment in that venture is expected to exceed

00:07:08.222 --> 00:07:14.082
$23 billion. TSMC's Japan account said output and spending would come in phases,

00:07:14.522 --> 00:07:19.662
following market demand, and only with Japanese government support in place. A separate

00:07:19.662 --> 00:07:25.142
August agreement with Sony semiconductor solutions created advanced vision semiconductor manufacturing

00:07:25.142 --> 00:07:32.044
in Kumamoto for next-generation image sensors. Reuters reports as an exclusive that bite-dance,

00:07:32.224 --> 00:07:38.724
Alibaba, and Tencent have placed more than $35 billion of NVIDIA chip orders. Those are orders

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:45.480
placed not chips the story describes as delivered. Biggo Finance citing the Alec also reports today

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:51.600
that Elon Musk first tried to buy plans from Intel, TSMC, and Micron, was turned down

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:57.220
and moved tariffab onto partnerships, with Intel contributing its 14A process and must

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:03.280
capping TSMC at a subcontractor role at most. A ruling party lawmaker in South Korea has

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:08.360
attacked a planned AI data center grid code, and asked for an exemption for projects already

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:14.620
underway. The Register reports tens of thousands of NVIDIA GPUs in Meta's Prometheus supercluster

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:17.180
are sitting idle, kept ready for a failure.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:20.040
Data Center Dynamics reports shade forms,

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.680
flex VMs turn bare metal GPU clusters

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:25.540
into single tenant virtual machines on its marketplace,

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:28.940
and that an approved node can be enrolled in about 30 minutes.

00:08:29.780 --> 00:08:32.020
Digitimes reports control and FSE

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:34.340
are combining laser and plasma processes

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.500
for advanced packaging.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.720
Pulse 2.0 reports Apple is expanding a $600 billion

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:44.040
US manufacturing plan with CUNITY, Perryman, Broadcom,

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.380
Corning, Coherent, TSMC, and AMCore.

00:08:48.198 --> 00:08:53.718
Co-packaged optics stalls in the factory when the fiber array has to find the dye without ever touching it.

00:08:54.578 --> 00:09:01.278
Semiconductor engineering's panel on scaling that test pass one dye treats fiber alignment as the bottleneck on the optical engine.

00:09:01.858 --> 00:09:05.558
The fiber array unit is meant to couple light and never contact the device.

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:08.178
Crash it and bring up and the array is damaged.

00:09:08.778 --> 00:09:13.538
Leave contamination on it and the reading is useless, so cleaning sits inside the test cell.

00:09:13.538 --> 00:09:20.738
Dave Armstrong of ISC Labs, part of ASC Group, draws the power limit, and 8kW GPU with

00:09:20.738 --> 00:09:25.418
connectors on several sides asks the tester to push that power in and pull the heat out,

00:09:25.838 --> 00:09:27.738
and that is already hard past one die.

00:09:28.378 --> 00:09:33.638
Matt Griffin at TeraDine says most production cells today are single-site, and that multi-site

00:09:33.638 --> 00:09:36.678
probe cards would ease fiber alignment if they actually work.

00:09:37.298 --> 00:09:40.998
Ira Leventhal at Advanced uses the ball grid array as the warning.

00:09:40.998 --> 00:09:44.318
Socket apart too many times, and the balls are at risk.

00:09:44.778 --> 00:09:49.878
The optical connector on the device is built to be mated once, and the hope is never unplugged.

00:09:50.258 --> 00:09:54.498
A test connector that survives 20-50 insertions is not a production tool.

00:09:54.958 --> 00:09:58.098
It needs tens of thousands of insertions or 100,000.

00:09:58.498 --> 00:10:03.318
The panel's answer is hardened metal on the tester side, mating to a device receptacle

00:10:03.318 --> 00:10:07.678
that is not hardened, so a rough mate can kill the device connector before its spec

00:10:07.678 --> 00:10:08.078
life.

00:10:08.078 --> 00:10:13.638
Kazuo Yamaguchi at Keysight splits the easy contact from the one that qualifies the engine.

00:10:14.158 --> 00:10:16.858
DC pads plus an optical probe are mechanical.

00:10:17.518 --> 00:10:23.118
Modulator and photo detector proof is S parameters, so light and high frequency radio frequency

00:10:23.118 --> 00:10:24.698
probes have to land together.

00:10:25.358 --> 00:10:30.618
Probe cards carry only so many radio frequency lines, and their bandwidth is limited, while

00:10:30.618 --> 00:10:33.418
these devices are characterized past 200 gigahertz.

00:10:33.418 --> 00:10:40.738
11th all adds warpage. Alignment has to hold on several axes from the top or the side, while a dense

00:10:40.738 --> 00:10:46.198
ball grid array still has to connect. Griffin's package map puts an optical face and an electrical

00:10:46.198 --> 00:10:52.778
face on every insertion. Sometimes top, sometimes bottom, sometimes both, and at module level on two

00:10:52.778 --> 00:10:58.598
to four sides across several optical engines. Optical alignment alone, he says, is not the hard part.

00:10:58.598 --> 00:11:02.758
doing it on every face at once with power and radio frequency is.

00:11:03.258 --> 00:11:08.358
Walk Armstrong's Split, the 8kW GPU with connectors on several sides already

00:11:08.358 --> 00:11:13.138
strains one tester insertion, so a second sight buys nothing if the tester cannot

00:11:13.138 --> 00:11:18.318
feed it. Photonic integrated circuit wafer test in his experience is single-site

00:11:18.318 --> 00:11:23.918
now with a chance to rise if probe card makers, and he names Technoprobe, can put

00:11:23.918 --> 00:11:30.038
more optical sights on one card. Near-packaged optics is usually one connector. High volume

00:11:30.038 --> 00:11:34.818
of that class forces multi-site because one alignment per tester hour will not clear

00:11:34.818 --> 00:11:40.678
the line. He calls insertions 2 and 3 the fertile ground. The long insertions where multi-site

00:11:40.678 --> 00:11:46.358
can take timeout. Single-site stays rational while that 8 kilowatt ASIC still exceeds what

00:11:46.358 --> 00:11:51.158
the tester can give a second die, while each site still needs its own clean fiber array

00:11:51.158 --> 00:11:56.478
that must not touch the die, and while the measurement that matters is an electro-optic

00:11:56.478 --> 00:12:02.078
S-parameter past 200 gigahertz that a probe card cannot fan out, it stops being the right

00:12:02.078 --> 00:12:07.378
cell when the product is a single connector near-packaged engine in high volume, insertions

00:12:07.378 --> 00:12:13.078
2 and 3 own the test time, and a hardened test connector can survive on the order of 100,000

00:12:13.078 --> 00:12:15.958
matings without destroying the softer receptacle on the part.

00:12:15.958 --> 00:12:23.223
On the horizon, construction of fab-22 phase-4 in Kausheng is set to finish next year, on a site

00:12:23.223 --> 00:12:28.783
whose steel work is now stopped. Commercial production at the TSMC and Sony Image Sensor Venture

00:12:28.783 --> 00:12:35.203
in Kumamoto is scheduled for 2029. Amazon's Germany pledge, including data center expansion,

00:12:35.503 --> 00:12:43.343
is dated to 2027. And Dell does not expect meaningful new memory fab supply until 2029 or 2030.

00:12:43.343 --> 00:12:49.237
Before we go, watch whether labor inspectors in Kaohsiung assign liability for the snapped

00:12:49.237 --> 00:12:50.397
connecting plate bolts.

00:12:51.037 --> 00:12:53.197
That's AI chips and data centers for today.

